  "citations": [
    {
      "id": "tax.us.2025.citation.schedule8812.part-i",
      "version": "v1"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "On a joint return with a counted child whose own SSN is valid: the other spouse's SSN or ITIN by the due date (spouse-ssn-or-itin) is required. When the taxpayer's SSN is not valid, the spouse's valid SSN is the filer gate's answer instead, and this gate asks nothing more. Other filing statuses and no counted child need no spouse answer."
